If you try to use table tags in the hits widget template like this:

`search.addWidget(
        instantsearch.widgets.hits({
          container: '#hits-container',
          templates: {
            empty: 'No events found',
            item: '<tr><td><a href="{{view_uri}}">{{event_number}}</a></td><td><a href="{{view_uri}}" target="_new">{{name}}</a></td><td>{{startdaypart_name}}</td><td>{{duration_name}}</td><td>{{room_name}}</td><td><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-info-sign" data-toggle="tooltip" title="{{description}}"></span></td></tr>'
          },
        })
      );`

You'll get this error:

**Minified exception occurred; use the non-minified dev environment for the full error message and additional helpful warnings.**

Here's a JS Fiddle that shows it happening.

https://jsfiddle.net/qkqzgsv9/

I've documented my process for finding this on this stack overflow question:  http://stackoverflow.com/questions/34515559/algolia-instantsearch-js-minified-exception-occurred-invariant

It doesn't happen if you use `div` tags rather than `tr` and `td` tags
